  "remainderPart": "plate-remainder",
  "coverage": {
    "declarations": "External pinnae are anatomically absent. Four visible feet, exposed neck, beaked head and stub tail are hand-authored on the exact original.",
    "limitations": "Interior root/spine/pelvis/chest points are source-local control frames inside the shell, not seen bones. Far limb emergence under the shell is partly occluded; the far hip (hindFarRoot) sits at an interpreted position under the shell rim above the visible far thigh. a01 refused leg/torso:hindFar with the hip on the visible stub top; a02 static RED by presentation contact drift 0.25003 at hindFarAnkle with ankle landmarks on the ankle-part boundary, so a03 extended each ankle part 10px proximal (still RED 0.25001, foreFarAnkle); a04 makes each ankle part the whole visible foot block (~45-55px) with the ankle landmark in its interior, as in the qualified C215 tortoise reference, so the support vertex triangle is not at a part seam."
  }
